try-except program ko girne se bachata hai:

```python
try:
    n = int(input('Number dalo: '))
    print(100 / n)
except:
    print('Galat input ya zero dala gaya')
```

Agar user galti kare (jaise 0 daal de), program band hone ki jagah pyar se samjha dega — yahi try-except ka kaam hai.

