CSS me rang color se badalta hai:

```css
p {
  color: red;
}
```

Ye saare paragraph ka rang laal kar dega.

JavaScript me variable let se banta hai:

```javascript
let naam = 'Vishesh';
console.log(naam);
```

let se bana variable badla ja sakta hai, const se bana nahi badalta.

Background rang aise badalta hai:

```css
body {
  background-color: lightblue;
}
```

Font size aise badalta hai:

```css
h1 {
  font-size: 32px;
}
```

Button click par function chalane ke liye onclick use hota hai:

```html
<button onclick='namaste()'>Click karo</button>
<script>
function namaste() {
  alert('Namaste Boss!');
}
</script>
```

JavaScript me for loop aise likhte hain:

```javascript
for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
  console.log(i);
}
```

Ye 1, 2, 3 print karega.
